00:29:55.150 --> 00:29:55.870
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: sa nakaraang

asr-000569
00:29:55.870 --> 00:29:57.310
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: 2025 NEP

asr-000570
00:29:57.310 --> 00:29:58.390
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: pero yung pong

asr-000571
00:29:58.390 --> 00:29:59.250
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: sa GAA

asr-000572
00:29:59.250 --> 00:29:59.970
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: ito naman po

asr-000573
00:29:59.970 --> 00:30:00.010
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: ay

asr-000574
00:30:00.000 --> 00:30:05.900
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: pag-uusapan pa po ng House of Congress, both House, Lower House and Upper House.

asr-000575
00:30:05.900 --> 00:30:16.020
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Pero kung ikukumpara po natin yung ating 2026 NEP doon po sa nakaraang 2026 GAA, ito po yung mas mababa ng 21.2%.

asr-000576
00:30:16.020 --> 00:30:17.420
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Next slide po.

asr-000577
00:30:19.940 --> 00:30:28.060
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: So ito po yung breakdown naman according to our three buckets ng ating usual expense.

asr-000578
00:30:28.060 --> 00:30:44.060
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Ang PS po, which is the salaries and wages, personal salary PS, is at P218 billion, which is the largest share, and 20% higher than the previous 2026 NEP.

asr-000579
00:30:44.980 --> 00:30:50.120
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Ang ating pong, sorry, yung pula po ang maintenance and other operating expense, sorry po, MOOE po yun.

asr-000580
00:30:50.660 --> 00:30:57.040
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Ang nakasama din po yung capital, yung pong ating mga GOCC hospitals at DOH hospitals.

asr-000581
00:30:57.040 --> 00:31:01.340
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Ang personal service po ay 7% higher than 2026 NEP.

asr-000582
00:31:01.760 --> 00:31:07.760
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: At ang capital outlay, ito po yung medyo bumaba kumpara po nung nakaraang 2026 NEP.

asr-000583
00:31:08.340 --> 00:31:17.960
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Ito po ay composed ng P14.5 billion for HPEP and P4.2 billion po doon sa Health System Resilience Project na ito po ay loan natin sa World Bank.

asr-000584
00:31:18.180 --> 00:31:23.180
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: At nakalaan sa 17 probinsya po na identified na nitong World Bank loan natin.

asr-000585
00:31:23.720 --> 00:31:24.500
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Next slide po.

asr-000586
00:31:24.500 --> 00:31:35.420
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Yung ating, kung ating pong i-divide na yung buong 353 budget po ng DOH, ito nga po yung limang pillars.

asr-000587
00:31:35.840 --> 00:31:39.580
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Yung para po doon sa unang pillar na Healthy School Workplace and Communities.

asr-000588
00:31:40.140 --> 00:31:48.820
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Ang malaking portion po dito, or 55.4 per billion, ay yung share po ng PhilHealth Premium to cover the indirect contributor.

asr-000589
00:31:48.820 --> 00:31:53.820
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: 30.7 million po ang aming nakalap na dami.

asr-000590
00:31:54.500 --> 00:31:56.800
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Ito po ng ating registered indirect contributor.

asr-000591
00:31:57.480 --> 00:31:59.820
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: P2.5 billion po for health promotion.

asr-000592
00:32:00.180 --> 00:32:08.120
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Short pa rin po ng mandated na 1%, but ito po ay tumaas na significantly compared ng mga nakaraang taon na halos dumoble.

asr-000593
00:32:08.760 --> 00:32:12.580
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: And then P1.3 billion po dito sa ating health emergency preparedness.

asr-000594
00:32:12.880 --> 00:32:18.960
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Dahil alam po natin, bunga nitong global warming, marami po tayo ngayong mga na-experience.

asr-000595
00:32:19.080 --> 00:32:24.180
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Kagaya nga po nitong haze, ito pong pagbaha, at saka po itong surge po.

asr-000596
00:32:24.500 --> 00:32:26.260
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Dengue at leptospirosis.

asr-000597
00:32:26.880 --> 00:32:27.420
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Next slide.

asr-000598
00:32:28.940 --> 00:32:33.180
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: So kung titignan naman po natin yung performance noong 2025,

asr-000599
00:32:33.860 --> 00:32:38.360
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: ang ating pong fully immunized ay 2 out of 3 children.

asr-000600
00:32:38.860 --> 00:32:42.120
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Ito po ay nasa 64.54%.

asr-000601
00:32:42.120 --> 00:32:46.140
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Hindi rin po ito umabot noong target natin na 95%.

asr-000602
00:32:46.140 --> 00:32:54.080
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: So ito po yung pinagtutuunan ko ng pansin, kasi karamihan po dito ay yung commodities po ay hindi dumating ng oras.

asr-000603
00:32:54.500 --> 00:32:57.920
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Para pagpambabakuna na inaayos na rin po natin.

asr-000604
00:32:58.460 --> 00:33:03.260
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: 8 out of 10 children, age 2 and below, had adequate height for their age.

asr-000605
00:33:03.340 --> 00:33:05.400
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: So ito po naman yung sukatan natin ng stunting.

asr-000606
00:33:05.400 --> 00:33:13.720
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: So ito po ay nasa 21.1% na ibaba na po natin kumpara noong 22.5% noong 2023.

asr-000607
00:33:14.360 --> 00:33:17.940
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: And then 8 out of 10 households had access to basic water supply.

asr-000608
00:33:18.640 --> 00:33:22.340
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Ito po ay 82.74% ng kabuang household.

asr-000609
00:33:22.820 --> 00:33:24.360
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Medyo falling short pa rin po.

asr-000610
00:33:24.500 --> 00:33:27.220
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Yung 25 target na 94%.

asr-000611
00:33:27.220 --> 00:33:31.560
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: At 7 out of 10 Filipinos had access to family planning needs.

asr-000612
00:33:32.000 --> 00:33:34.900
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Ito po ay nasa 72.5%.

asr-000613
00:33:34.900 --> 00:33:38.900
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: So ito po ay nahigitan yung ating target na 64.5%.

asr-000614
00:33:38.900 --> 00:33:43.260
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Ang ating pong nabigyan ng TB meds ay 367,000.

asr-000615
00:33:43.580 --> 00:33:47.680
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: At ito po ay 85% po ng ating accomplishment, which is our target.

asr-000616
00:33:47.940 --> 00:33:51.300
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: At accomplishment target na na-achieve naman po natin.

asr-000617
00:33:51.800 --> 00:33:53.600
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: At 100,000 po ang Pilipino.

asr-000618
00:33:53.600 --> 00:33:58.180
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: At higit 100,000 po, living with HIV, ang nakatanggap po ng treatment.

asr-000619
00:33:58.740 --> 00:34:03.640
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: At ito po ay 66% accomplishment versus our target of 70%.

asr-000620
00:34:03.640 --> 00:34:09.740
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: 15,000 cancer patients po ang naka-access ng ating essential medicines and palliative care.

asr-000621
00:34:10.140 --> 00:34:16.580
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: At 262,000 individuals naman po ang nakatanggap po ng mental health medicines and intervention.

asr-000622
00:34:17.460 --> 00:34:18.400
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Next slide please.

asr-000623
00:34:19.340 --> 00:34:23.400
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Sa ating pong PILAR 2, which is the Functional Primary Care Services,

asr-000624
00:34:23.600 --> 00:34:30.740
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: system, 9.1 billion po ang for family health, immunization, nutrition, and responsible parenting.

asr-000625
00:34:30.740 --> 00:34:34.540
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: So tinahina po namin ito ngayon doon sa ating YACA program,

asr-000626
00:34:34.900 --> 00:34:41.100
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: kung saan po papalawigin din eventually na magkaroon din ang access doon sa ating commodities for family planning.

asr-000627
00:34:41.620 --> 00:34:44.200
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Ang communicable disease, 6.9 billion.

asr-000628
00:34:44.500 --> 00:34:47.300
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: At nakasentro po ito sa TB at HIV.

asr-000629
00:34:47.780 --> 00:34:53.580
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Again, nag-uusap na po kami ni PCO Bevho kung paano din po maisama itong mga commodities.

asr-000630
00:34:53.600 --> 00:35:00.840
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Sa ating YACAP gamot at para rin din po makover yung ating testing ng HIV.

asr-000631
00:35:01.580 --> 00:35:08.740
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Yung 2.7 billion po ay for non-communicable diseases, which includes hypertension, diabetes, mental health.

asr-000632
00:35:08.900 --> 00:35:12.780
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Again, ito po ay isasama din ni Doktora Bev sa pagpapalawak ng gamot.

asr-000633
00:35:13.380 --> 00:35:16.980
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: At 1.5 billion for local health systems development.

asr-000634
00:35:18.240 --> 00:35:22.980
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Upang suportahan po yung 18 regyon, lalong-lalo na po yung 110 UHM.

asr-000635
00:35:23.600 --> 00:35:26.180
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Next slide, please.

asr-000636
00:35:27.540 --> 00:35:31.600
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Dito naman po sa Pillar 3, which is the quality and efficient hospitals.

asr-000637
00:35:32.420 --> 00:35:39.620
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Nakita po natin na nung nakaraang taon, record high pong 300 billion ang benefit payment na nailabas ng PhilHealth.

asr-000638
00:35:39.940 --> 00:35:42.600
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Ito po ay 82% increase from the previous year.

asr-000639
00:35:43.800 --> 00:35:50.740
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Na nagpapatunay nga po kung bakit bumaba yung out-of-pocket spending ng mga Pilipino nung nakaraang taong 2025.

asr-000640
00:35:51.580 --> 00:35:53.480
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Out of the 300 billion,

asr-000641
00:35:53.600 --> 00:35:59.520
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: kasama na po yung 40 million na Pilipinos registered with the YACAP nung nakaraang taon po.

asr-000642
00:36:00.420 --> 00:36:03.720
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Yung pong nakatanggap ng ma-EFIP ay 4.3 million.

asr-000643
00:36:04.260 --> 00:36:09.220
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Out of which, 4.3 million patients in 2025.

asr-000644
00:36:09.840 --> 00:36:16.300
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: And then these are served, 32,000 plus patients served through e-MA-EFIP na po.

asr-000645
00:36:16.520 --> 00:36:18.700
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: So nagsishift na po tayo to e-MA-EFIP.

asr-000646
00:36:18.860 --> 00:36:20.220
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Pinupisaan lang po ito nung August.

asr-000647
00:36:21.320 --> 00:36:23.580
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: At sa mula po nung August, mag-iisang buwan.

asr-000648
00:36:23.580 --> 00:36:28.600
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: At sa mula pa lang po, 32,000 na po ang dito natin na i-process sa e-MA-EFIP.

asr-000649
00:36:28.940 --> 00:36:34.040
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: At kami po ay nagpapalawig at atin pong inumpisahan sa DOH hospitals.

asr-000650
00:36:34.160 --> 00:36:38.200
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Ngayon po ay isasama na po natin yung mga local government unit hospitals.

asr-000651
00:36:38.520 --> 00:36:41.480
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: At nakita naman po na mas mabilis na po yung ating processing.

asr-000652
00:36:42.240 --> 00:36:46.060
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: 54,000 cancer patients po ang nakareceive ng Cancer Assistance Fund.

asr-000653
00:36:46.640 --> 00:36:52.780
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Nearly 2,000 health infrastructure projects were completed in the last 2 years, 3 years, 23 to 25.

asr-000654
00:36:53.580 --> 00:36:56.180
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: And almost 5,000 medical equipments were procured.

asr-000655
00:36:56.440 --> 00:37:01.960
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Lahat po ito kasaming 500 medical transport vehicles are done through our HVEP.

asr-000656
00:37:02.660 --> 00:37:03.680
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Next slide please.

asr-000657
00:37:05.790 --> 00:37:13.730
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: So ang nandito rin po sa Pillar 3 ay yung operations po ng ating 71 regional hospitals and health facilities.

asr-000658
00:37:13.730 --> 00:37:17.450
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Yung ating pong labindalwang DOH hospitals na karagdagan.

asr-000659
00:37:17.610 --> 00:37:21.110
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Ito pong 71 po ay sa region, 21 po ay sa Manila.

asr-000660
00:37:21.670 --> 00:37:24.430
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: At yung pong apat na specialty hospital.

asr-000661
00:37:24.830 --> 00:37:31.450
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Na nandito po ang Lung Center, NKTI, Philippine Heart Center, and Philippine Children's Medical Center.

asr-000662
00:37:31.910 --> 00:37:42.310
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Lahat po na nabigyan po ng ating NEP ng kaukulang coverage po ng kanilang MOOE at PS.

asr-000663
00:37:42.310 --> 00:37:48.670
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: So karamihan po dito sa MOOE ay ginagamit po para ma-maintain po yung ating Z-BEN package.

asr-000664
00:37:48.810 --> 00:37:54.130
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Kasi yan po yung nagsusustena nung kanilang quantified free service o yung pong sumosobra.

asr-000665
00:37:54.830 --> 00:38:05.660
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Ito po yung coverage ng PhilHealth at ng initial 55 billion na nabanggit ko kanina.

asr-000666
00:38:06.160 --> 00:38:11.740
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: At ito po ay para palawigin along 11 diseases po na nakalinya na dun sa aming roadmap.

asr-000667
00:38:12.720 --> 00:38:16.500
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Again, yung MAIFI po nabigyan ng 24.2 billion.

asr-000668
00:38:16.500 --> 00:38:20.780
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Ang Cancer Assistance Fund ay nabigyan ulit po ng 3.8 billion.

asr-000669
00:38:20.920 --> 00:38:22.340
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Medyo mas mataas ng nakaraang taon.

asr-000670
00:38:22.840 --> 00:38:31.060
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: At yung HPEP nga po, bagamat nabawasan, meron pa rin pong 14.5 na ikinocover nga po yung ating 500.

asr-000671
00:38:31.100 --> 00:38:37.420
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: 114 health facilities, 845 equipment projects, and 345 medical transport vehicles.

asr-000672
00:38:37.720 --> 00:38:44.680
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: So ito po yung aming iapila na i-considera po ng ating appropriations or finance committee po

asr-000673
00:38:44.680 --> 00:38:53.220
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: na kung pwede pong maibalik dahil po ito'y napaka-importante para nga po palakasin natin yung ating services sa local government unit

asr-000674
00:38:53.220 --> 00:38:57.780
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: para hindi po dumadagsa at nabubulunan itong ating mga DOH hospitals.

asr-000675
00:38:58.500 --> 00:38:59.320
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Next slide po.

asr-000676
00:39:00.100 --> 00:39:00.680
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: So yung pillar 4.

asr-000677
00:39:01.100 --> 00:39:03.260
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: 4 po ay sa information technology.

asr-000678
00:39:03.480 --> 00:39:09.060
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Gaya ng nasabi ko, talagang titignan po natin na magkaroon na po ng central digital health system

asr-000679
00:39:09.060 --> 00:39:12.060
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: kung saan nga po merong health information exchange.

asr-000680
00:39:12.640 --> 00:39:19.340
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: 480 billion po for epidemiology and surveillance, and 222 million po for health statistics

asr-000681
00:39:19.340 --> 00:39:25.280
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: na tinitrack din po natin para matiyak na yung pong ating nagawa ay nagbubunga.

asr-000682
00:39:25.420 --> 00:39:30.860
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Gaya ng nasabi ko sa una, something that is not captured data does not exist.

asr-000683
00:39:31.100 --> 00:39:32.900
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: And next slide po.

asr-000684
00:39:33.140 --> 00:39:38.260
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Sa pillar 5, sa ating strong institutions, workforce, and sector.

asr-000685
00:39:38.900 --> 00:39:43.440
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: So tayo po ay itutuloy yung National Health Workforce Support System.

asr-000686
00:39:43.620 --> 00:39:50.600
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Ito po yung karagdagang health professionals na dinideploy natin sa iba-ibang mga province at local government unit.

asr-000687
00:39:50.820 --> 00:39:55.580
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Meron po tayong naka-plano pong 24,381 health professionals.

asr-000688
00:39:55.580 --> 00:40:01.080
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: At yung ating supply chain management na akin din po tinitingnan kung paano po,

asr-000689
00:40:01.100 --> 00:40:07.700
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: i-revive yung ating mga digital systems na di umano yung ano na po, outdated na daw.

asr-000690
00:40:08.060 --> 00:40:10.720
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Pero titingnan ko po kung paano po ito i-update.

asr-000691
00:40:11.180 --> 00:40:16.320
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Kasama na rin po dito yung pagbiminta na po ng warehouse at saka yung cold chain po

asr-000692
00:40:16.320 --> 00:40:21.900
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: para nga po dito sa ating mga bakuna at para matiyak po na hindi po nasasayang

asr-000693
00:40:21.900 --> 00:40:26.900
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: dahil mamaintain po natin yung quality nung pag-re-store nitong ating gamot at bakuna.

asr-000694
00:40:27.540 --> 00:40:28.360
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Next slide.

asr-000695
00:40:29.220 --> 00:40:31.060
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: So yun po ang budget po

asr-000696
00:40:31.100 --> 00:40:36.840
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: At ang budget po ng ating departamento and its attached agency at bilang isang health sector

asr-000697
00:40:36.840 --> 00:40:45.940
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: ang ating pinagtutunan ngayon po ay internally una sa pagtutulungan, una sa pag-usad, una sa pagkilala

asr-000698
00:40:45.940 --> 00:40:52.020
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: dahil ang aking push ay hindi siya siloed at dapat nag-uusap-usap lahat ng sector within the

asr-000699
00:40:52.020 --> 00:40:54.700
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: all the agencies within the health sector.

asr-000700
00:40:54.700 --> 00:41:01.080
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Para po ito maramdaman ng ating taong bayan isang mabilis, patas at mapagkakatiwala ang health sector.

asr-000701
00:41:01.100 --> 00:41:02.980
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Maraming maraming salamat po.

asr-000702
00:41:03.000 --> 00:41:25.000
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you, Secretary Mercado. At this juncture, the Chair would like to acknowledge the presence of our Senate President Win Gatchalian. Thank you, sir, for joining us. The Chair would like to already ask our PhilHealth: Do you have any presentation? Ah kasama na? Oo nga pala, no? Nandun naman po yung

asr-000702-split-2
00:41:25.000 --> 00:41:25.630
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: United na.

asr-000702-split-3
00:41:25.630 --> 00:41:26.160
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Yes po.

asr-000702-split-4
00:41:26.160 --> 00:41:36.820
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Kasi dati nag-aaway pa yung [unclear], magsusuntukan pa eh. At least I'm happy now that we'll have a better chance of implementation kasi magkasama na.

asr-000703
00:41:36.860 --> 00:41:38.120
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Unified na ang program.

asr-000704
00:41:39.120 --> 00:41:40.940
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Okay, any agencies pa?

asr-000705
00:41:41.140 --> 00:41:43.380
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So we can probably start already, no?

asr-000706
00:41:43.440 --> 00:41:47.400
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Siguro we'll just ask the other agencies and attached corporations later.

asr-000707
00:41:48.140 --> 00:41:53.720
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So in order of arrival, Senator Lacson, but our Senate President, would you like to go ahead?

asr-000708
00:41:55.720 --> 00:42:00.740
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: I'll waive my seniority in rank.

asr-000709
00:42:01.100 --> 00:42:03.660
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Senator Lacson, may now ask the questions.

asr-000710
00:42:04.040 --> 00:42:07.040
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Thank you, Mr. Chairman, and good morning to the DOH family.

asr-000711
00:42:08.020 --> 00:42:10.900
Senator Panfilo Lacson: And congratulations kay Secretary Mercado.

asr-000712
00:42:11.680 --> 00:42:17.720
Senator Panfilo Lacson: I've been receiving positive feedback sa pagka-appoint ninyo sa mga nakakilala sa inyo.

asr-000713
00:42:20.380 --> 00:42:28.020
Senator Panfilo Lacson: As I mentioned earlier, Mr. Chairman, mag-focus po yung aking mga tanong sa Universal Healthcare Act na ipinasan ninyo.

asr-000714
00:42:28.020 --> 00:42:31.020
Senator Panfilo Lacson: You have championed this law.

asr-000715
00:42:31.100 --> 00:42:43.240
Senator Panfilo Lacson: So since 2017, 18th Congress, until we enacted it into law in 2019, at saka nag-rollout tayo 2020.

asr-000716
00:42:44.380 --> 00:42:51.400
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Ang isang napansin ko lang, since na-rollout, lagi pong papalit-palit yung ating spending plans.

asr-000717
00:42:52.320 --> 00:42:58.220
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Kaya ang unang tanong ko, where are we at in the implementation of the Universal Healthcare Act?

asr-000718
00:42:59.380 --> 00:43:01.080
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Kasi po, pupunta namin.

asr-000719
00:43:01.100 --> 00:43:02.560
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Medium, babalik tayo ng low.

asr-000720
00:43:03.400 --> 00:43:05.220
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Hanggang ngayon, wala pa po tayo doon sa high.

asr-000721
00:43:06.140 --> 00:43:14.840
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Yung six years, diba, ang timeline yan, ang pag-aalam ko po, after six years, which ito na yan, 2020, 2026,

asr-000722
00:43:15.020 --> 00:43:19.020
Senator Panfilo Lacson: dapat nasa high-end na tayo, ang coverage, lahat na.

asr-000723
00:43:19.340 --> 00:43:20.540
Senator Panfilo Lacson: So nasaan po tayo ngayon?

asr-000724
00:43:22.280 --> 00:43:23.700
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

asr-000725
00:43:25.880 --> 00:43:30.980
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Medyo noong po no-launch, nagkaroon po ng, hindi inaasahang COVID.

asr-000726
00:43:31.100 --> 00:43:34.080
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Kaya po, medyo na-delay yung ating implementation.

asr-000727
00:43:35.240 --> 00:43:37.820
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Medyo na-pushback ng two to even three years.

asr-000728
00:43:38.800 --> 00:43:42.900
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Yung pong universal coverage, kung yun po yung pagtutuunan, na-achieve po yun.

asr-000729
00:43:43.060 --> 00:43:45.580
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Kasi immediate eligibility na po lahat ng Pilipino.

asr-000730
00:43:46.000 --> 00:43:48.840
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: So hindi na po yung kung meron ka lang hulog, siya haka mako-cover.

asr-000731
00:43:49.580 --> 00:43:57.320
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Ang kaso po, yung supply side, yung pong nagbibigay ng mga benepisyo, yung pa po yung kailangan nating pagtuunan.

asr-000732
00:43:57.320 --> 00:44:00.320
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Kasi hindi pa rin po equal yung presence ng mga...

asr-000733
00:44:01.100 --> 00:44:05.380
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: accredited health facilities ng PhilHealth na magbigay.

asr-000734
00:44:05.480 --> 00:44:10.220
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Lalo na po yung mga matataas na uri po ng sakit na meron na naman pong coverage.

asr-000735
00:44:10.560 --> 00:44:11.980
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Pero wala pong mga capabilities.

asr-000736
00:44:12.240 --> 00:44:17.280
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Open heart surgery, renal transplant, at mga matataas pa pong mga procedures

asr-000737
00:44:17.280 --> 00:44:21.000
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: ng covered ng Z-package ng PhilHealth.

asr-000738
00:44:21.500 --> 00:44:26.340
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Doon po naman sa mga local government units, medyo doon din po nahuulay.

asr-000739
00:44:26.340 --> 00:44:30.520
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Kasi supposedly po, dahil with the devolved nature of our UHC law,

asr-000740
00:44:30.520 --> 00:44:37.340
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: ay natuturoan na po sila how to run their local health systems.

asr-000741
00:44:37.840 --> 00:44:39.520
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: May maturity grading po tayo.

asr-000742
00:44:39.780 --> 00:44:42.200
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Almost 110 na naman pong probinsya.

asr-000743
00:44:42.620 --> 00:44:46.040
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Ang talagang 110 provinces na nga po.

asr-000744
00:44:46.320 --> 00:44:50.380
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Ang medyo nag-re-reach na po ng maturity.

asr-000745
00:44:50.620 --> 00:44:55.760
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: So ngayon po, nagsishift na kami na ang payment po ay pumunta na doon sa isang special healthcare fund

asr-000746
00:44:55.760 --> 00:44:59.680
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: para mapagplanuhan po na mas mabuti ng ating local chief executive.

asr-000747
00:45:00.000 --> 00:45:13.440
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: sa kanila pong mga health budgets. Pero kailangan pa po ng tulong kasi nga po una na po dyan di pa rin pare-pareho yung kakayanan ng ating mga local health units na papondohan yung kanilang healthcare.

asr-000748
00:45:13.440 --> 00:45:30.240
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Kaya po yung PhilHealth na nagpalawig ng kanilang coverage noong nakaraan to, malaki pong tulong. Kaya marami naman pong mga local health office o mga LCEs ang lumalapit na ngayon medyo kaya-kaya nila dahil kumikita na yung kanilang mga hospital at clinic.

asr-000749
00:45:30.240 --> 00:45:38.700
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: So matter lang po of turuan how to budget and how to allocate properly. At yun nga po yung tinitingnan naming tulungan yung mga LGUs.

asr-000750
00:45:39.160 --> 00:45:42.880
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: So in short po, hindi pa po natin na-achieve.

asr-000751
00:45:43.440 --> 00:45:54.260
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Hindi ko lang po mabibigyan yung actual percentage base po dun sa ating targets kasi nga po medyo yung mga nangyaring ventrics nag-iba-iba through the years.

asr-000752
00:45:54.260 --> 00:46:13.340
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: But yun nga po yung aking plano, sabi ko kay Dr. Bev, na this year by 2028 dapat yung mga local health units or yung local chief executive may mga sarili-sarili ng kanilang SHF at magkaroon na po kami ng proper financing analysis kung magkano po yung talagang kailangan.

asr-000753
00:46:13.440 --> 00:46:15.840
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Para talagang ma-achieve po yung universal healthcare.

asr-000754
00:46:15.840 --> 00:46:17.720
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Thank you, Secretary.

asr-000755
00:46:18.360 --> 00:46:26.660
Senator Panfilo Lacson: If I may, Mr. Chairman, i-plus ko lang sa screen yung ito yung papalit-palit na yung three spending plans noong 2022.

asr-000756
00:46:27.020 --> 00:46:35.420
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Ayan po, maliwanag na hindi po negligible yung mga figures. Medyo malalaki ito, mga substantial.

asr-000757
00:46:36.380 --> 00:46:43.420
Senator Panfilo Lacson: So ano yung practical purpose ng financing strategies kung palit tayo ng palit ng target?

asr-000758
00:46:43.440 --> 00:46:51.260
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Or nami-miss natin yung target. So probably we may need some more serious study.

asr-000759
00:46:52.600 --> 00:47:06.200
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Kasi kung lagi natin nami-miss yung target, para saan pa itong ating ginagawang financing strategies? Thank you.

asr-000760
00:47:08.200 --> 00:47:18.980
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: Chair, sir, as of now, we are tracking our total health expenditure and siguro yung good na nangyari po is,

asr-000761
00:47:19.200 --> 00:47:31.100
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: if you look at from 2022 to until now, 2025, yung share po ng PhilHealth, tumaas na po to 19% of total health expenditure.

asr-000762
00:47:31.880 --> 00:47:37.220
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: And the whole government share is up to 46.5%.

asr-000763
00:47:37.220 --> 00:47:44.580
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: So we have actually managed to reduce out-of-pocket payment share to at 41% by end of 2025.

asr-000764
00:47:44.580 --> 00:47:48.920
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: So to a certain extent, parang may malaki na yung progress.

asr-000765
00:47:49.200 --> 00:47:52.500
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: Kumpara sa 10 years ago, that that's around 55%.

asr-000766
00:47:52.500 --> 00:48:00.220
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: But Sen, we agree with you po that we have to recalibrate this kasi every three years nagbabago.

asr-000767
00:48:00.220 --> 00:48:16.220
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: But we are now following the PDP plan, which has a target of reducing our OOP to 37% by 2028.

asr-000768
00:48:16.360 --> 00:48:18.700
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: So 2025 at 41%.

asr-000769
00:48:18.700 --> 00:48:19.160
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: 2022.

asr-000770
00:48:19.200 --> 00:48:21.560
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: 2028 at 37%.

asr-000771
00:48:21.560 --> 00:48:27.220
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: And kung ipa-follow po natin yung initial projections dito po sa PDP,

asr-000772
00:48:27.700 --> 00:48:34.180
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: that amount should be at around 639 billion.

asr-000773
00:48:34.180 --> 00:48:39.360
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: So medyo aligned naman po sa number na ito, mas mataas lang po ng konti.

asr-000774
00:48:39.740 --> 00:48:43.880
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: So sir, yun po yung target namin po ni SEC na ma-achieve po.

asr-000775
00:48:44.040 --> 00:48:44.320
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: Thank you.

asr-000776
00:48:44.320 --> 00:48:44.580
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Thank you.

asr-000777
00:48:44.840 --> 00:48:48.340
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Pakibalik lang yung table doon sa CHE.

asr-000778
00:48:48.340 --> 00:48:51.040
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Current health expenditure kanina.

asr-000779
00:48:52.040 --> 00:49:00.080
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Yung, of course, maganda accomplishment, kasi malaki yung nabawas doon sa out-of-pocket yung household out-of-pocket payment.

asr-000780
00:49:00.400 --> 00:49:02.320
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Nasa 41.2%.

asr-000781
00:49:02.320 --> 00:49:05.860
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Dati po ba, ilang percent ito?

asr-000782
00:49:06.640 --> 00:49:09.360
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: Sir, 10 years ago, this was at 55%.

asr-000783
00:49:09.360 --> 00:49:09.560
Senator Panfilo Lacson: 55.

asr-000784
00:49:10.540 --> 00:49:12.560
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Pero ako gusto ko lang ma-educate.

asr-000785
00:49:12.560 --> 00:49:17.700
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Kasi pag sinabi natin government schemes and compulsory contributory health care,

asr-000786
00:49:17.700 --> 00:49:21.040
Senator Panfilo Lacson: financing schemes at 46%,

asr-000787
00:49:21.040 --> 00:49:23.940
Senator Panfilo Lacson: ano po ba ito?

asr-000788
00:49:24.240 --> 00:49:29.100
Senator Panfilo Lacson: What would constitute itong schemes na ito?

asr-000789
00:49:29.740 --> 00:49:34.400
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: Chair, it's national government spend, local government spend, and PhilHealth po.

asr-000790
00:49:35.240 --> 00:49:39.580
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Kasama na rito yung mga earmark na naka-incorporate sa GAA.

asr-000791
00:49:39.920 --> 00:49:43.580
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Kasi doon sa latest Supreme Court ruling,

asr-000792
00:49:44.280 --> 00:49:47.680
Senator Panfilo Lacson: while naka-earmark ito sa Department of Health,

asr-000793
00:49:47.700 --> 00:49:51.780
Senator Panfilo Lacson: hindi naman ito actually, pero nasa GAA yan, nakapasok.

asr-000794
00:49:52.020 --> 00:49:55.040
Senator Panfilo Lacson: So kasama rin ito dito sa 805 billion.

asr-000795
00:49:55.640 --> 00:49:56.400
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Lahat-lahat yan.

asr-000796
00:49:57.280 --> 00:50:02.260
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Including the National Expenditure Program na naging GAA.

asr-000797
00:50:03.020 --> 00:50:06.220
Senator Panfilo Lacson: So sa tingin ko po, hindi masyadong, sa akin lang,

asr-000798
00:50:06.520 --> 00:50:09.340
Senator Panfilo Lacson: yung misleading may be a wrong word,

asr-000799
00:50:09.460 --> 00:50:14.980
Senator Panfilo Lacson: but for the lack of a better word, I will just use it na misleading.

asr-000800
00:50:14.980 --> 00:50:16.780
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Parang, okay.

asr-000801
00:50:17.700 --> 00:50:24.020
Senator Panfilo Lacson: 46.5%, pero ito yung contributory health care financing schemes ng gobyerno.

asr-000802
00:50:24.800 --> 00:50:30.280
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Pero masyadong bloated, ikanga, kasi kasama na dyan yung PS.

asr-000803
00:50:31.040 --> 00:50:31.940
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Lahat-lahat eh, di ba?

asr-000804
00:50:32.040 --> 00:50:37.420
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Kasi pag sinabi nating General Appropriations Act na ito yung items under the DOH budget,

asr-000805
00:50:39.400 --> 00:50:43.720
Senator Panfilo Lacson: pagka nilimit lang natin sa health care program,

asr-000806
00:50:44.080 --> 00:50:45.800
Senator Panfilo Lacson: lilit yung 46.5.

asr-000807
00:50:46.440 --> 00:50:46.960
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Hindi po ba?

asr-000808
00:50:47.700 --> 00:50:53.320
Senator Panfilo Lacson: So ang target natin actually is to reduce further the household out-of-pocket.

asr-000809
00:50:53.400 --> 00:50:54.140
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Ito yung masakit eh.

asr-000810
00:50:54.680 --> 00:50:56.360
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Ito yung target ng UHC.

asr-000811
00:50:57.060 --> 00:50:59.920
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Yung out-of-pocket talaga, halos, huwag naman masiro.

asr-000812
00:51:00.120 --> 00:51:02.040
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Palagay ko, hindi natin kaya in our lifetime.

asr-000813
00:51:02.460 --> 00:51:06.140
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Pero medyo mataas pa yung 41.2%.

asr-000814
00:51:06.140 --> 00:51:10.300
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Yung voluntary health care payment schemes, partly government din ito eh.

asr-000815
00:51:10.360 --> 00:51:14.400
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Like in the Senate, meron kaming Kaiser, government funds din eh.

asr-000816
00:51:14.400 --> 00:51:15.960
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Yung pambayad ng premium.

asr-000817
00:51:16.580 --> 00:51:17.520
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Ang siguro,

asr-000818
00:51:17.700 --> 00:51:20.900
Senator Panfilo Lacson: papupuwera lang dito yung mga corporations, private corporations,

asr-000819
00:51:21.440 --> 00:51:26.900
Senator Panfilo Lacson: na meron silang sariling health benefits sa kanilang mga employees, sa kanilang mga staff.

asr-000820
00:51:27.780 --> 00:51:28.940
Senator Panfilo Lacson: So, yun.

asr-000821
00:51:30.840 --> 00:51:35.820
Senator Panfilo Lacson: I'd like to think na hindi, in practical terms,

asr-000822
00:51:36.400 --> 00:51:40.360
Senator Panfilo Lacson: hindi ito talagang ganung ka-accurate, yung 46.5.

asr-000823
00:51:40.740 --> 00:51:41.080
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Now,

asr-000824
00:51:44.280 --> 00:51:46.320
Senator Panfilo Lacson: anyway, yung mga earmarks, ano,

asr-000825
00:51:46.740 --> 00:51:47.680
Senator Panfilo Lacson: marami tayong mga,

asr-000826
00:51:47.700 --> 00:51:48.920
Senator Panfilo Lacson: mga specials na naipasa.

asr-000827
00:51:49.780 --> 00:51:53.000
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Gusto ko lang pong makakita ng medyo accurate, no?

asr-000828
00:51:53.140 --> 00:51:55.900
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Maski mga ballpark lang, hindi naman talaga detalyado.

asr-000829
00:51:56.320 --> 00:52:00.640
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Accounting ng mga funding source para sa UHC.

asr-000830
00:52:01.180 --> 00:52:02.540
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Like, for example, ano,

asr-000831
00:52:02.960 --> 00:52:06.020
Senator Panfilo Lacson: yung total incremental sin tax collection,

asr-000832
00:52:06.680 --> 00:52:10.360
Senator Panfilo Lacson: RA 10351, 2012 pa ito.

asr-000833
00:52:10.860 --> 00:52:14.880
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Tapos inamento ng tobacco tax law 2019, and so forth.

asr-000834
00:52:15.380 --> 00:52:17.680
Senator Panfilo Lacson: 50% nung national government,

asr-000835
00:52:17.700 --> 00:52:20.460
Senator Panfilo Lacson: government share from the income ng PAGCOR,

asr-000836
00:52:20.980 --> 00:52:22.780
Senator Panfilo Lacson: dyan din, naka-earmark din sa UHC.

asr-000837
00:52:23.460 --> 00:52:24.600
Senator Panfilo Lacson: So, meron po ba tayo?

asr-000838
00:52:24.700 --> 00:52:28.040
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Para lang magkaroon kami ng idea, kasi we're talking of the budget,

asr-000839
00:52:28.260 --> 00:52:30.120
Senator Panfilo Lacson: and these are, you know,

asr-000840
00:52:30.780 --> 00:52:34.060
Senator Panfilo Lacson: ang source nito talaga hindi naman revenues ng government,

asr-000841
00:52:34.520 --> 00:52:36.460
Senator Panfilo Lacson: kundi earmarks ito,

asr-000842
00:52:37.060 --> 00:52:40.780
Senator Panfilo Lacson: plus galing sa GOCC like PAGCOR, PCSO,

asr-000843
00:52:41.520 --> 00:52:43.000
Senator Panfilo Lacson: and so forth and so on.

asr-000844
00:52:43.380 --> 00:52:44.880
Senator Panfilo Lacson: So, meron po ba tayo yung ano nito?

asr-000845
00:52:45.680 --> 00:52:46.860
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Konting detalya lang.

asr-000846
00:52:53.910 --> 00:52:57.950
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: Share for PAGCOR and PCSO,

asr-000847
00:52:58.550 --> 00:53:01.430
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: based on our records,

asr-000848
00:53:01.730 --> 00:53:07.250
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: the total that we should be able to claim from 2019

asr-000849
00:53:07.250 --> 00:53:10.610
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: up to Q2 of 2026 should be

asr-000850
00:53:10.610 --> 00:53:14.550
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: P127.55 billion po.

asr-000851
00:53:15.830 --> 00:53:16.930
Senator Panfilo Lacson: 2019 to?

asr-000852
00:53:17.350 --> 00:53:18.330
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: 2026.

asr-000853
00:53:18.490 --> 00:53:19.190
Senator Panfilo Lacson: 2026.

asr-000854
00:53:19.590 --> 00:53:19.870
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: Opo.

asr-000855
00:53:19.870 --> 00:53:23.090
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: And then there was appropriation in,

asr-000856
00:53:23.910 --> 00:53:27.430
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: fiscal year 2023 GAA of 21 billion,

asr-000857
00:53:28.070 --> 00:53:32.410
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: and fiscal year 2024 GAA of 21 billion.

asr-000858
00:53:32.830 --> 00:53:36.090
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: So, for both of this, we have SARO already, but no.

asr-000859
00:53:36.710 --> 00:53:39.050
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Yeah, ang problema is naka-earmark,

asr-000860
00:53:39.990 --> 00:53:42.190
Senator Panfilo Lacson: nare-release ba talaga yung total amount na naka-earmark?

asr-000861
00:53:42.250 --> 00:53:43.450
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Yun ang problema natin.

asr-000862
00:53:44.350 --> 00:53:47.010
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Kasi on paper, magandang pakinggan yung,

asr-000863
00:53:47.590 --> 00:53:49.470
Senator Panfilo Lacson: eto yung 50% component

asr-000864
00:53:49.470 --> 00:53:53.690
Senator Panfilo Lacson: ng national government share, ano, from PAGCOR.

asr-000865
00:53:53.910 --> 00:53:57.710
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Pero yung, in real terms, yung nominal figure

asr-000866
00:53:57.710 --> 00:54:00.850
Senator Panfilo Lacson: ng 50% ng share ng government,

asr-000867
00:54:01.810 --> 00:54:03.550
Senator Panfilo Lacson: eh, dapat mapunta sa PAGCOR.

asr-000868
00:54:04.010 --> 00:54:06.070
Senator Panfilo Lacson: 50% ba talaga napunta sa PAGCOR?

asr-000869
00:54:06.230 --> 00:54:09.730
Senator Panfilo Lacson: I mean, sorry, sa DOH or sa universal healthcare.

asr-000870
00:54:10.770 --> 00:54:11.610
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Ano yung gap?

asr-000871
00:54:11.910 --> 00:54:15.430
Senator Panfilo Lacson: From all these special laws na naipasa,

asr-000872
00:54:15.870 --> 00:54:17.470
Senator Panfilo Lacson: na naka-earmark dapat sa DOH.

asr-000873
00:54:17.570 --> 00:54:19.610
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Of course, you understand na ito,

asr-000874
00:54:19.670 --> 00:54:21.670
Senator Panfilo Lacson: sa buong GAA ito pinapasok, hindi ba?

asr-000875
00:54:21.670 --> 00:54:23.830
Senator Panfilo Lacson: And you're dependent,

asr-000876
00:54:23.830 --> 00:54:25.210
Senator Panfilo Lacson: you're dependent on the DBM.

asr-000877
00:54:26.030 --> 00:54:29.250
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Kung magkano yung maibibigay lang para sa UHC?

asr-000878
